   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Backwards Jack** (1 review): The reviewer names this song as their personal favorite of the show [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **3rd Stone/unknown**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Backwards Jack**: back after 81 archived shows (1205 days) [4]\n- **Unconditional Love**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-12-30.akg483.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 132 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording one of the best Soulive tapings they've heard, capturing the band's full resonance [3]\n- **soulive2012-12-30.akg483.flac24**: source not stated; 13 songs; 132 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Mike Tucker joined on tenor saxophone for some songs, and Brian Thomas joined on trombone for others [1]\n- Mike Tucker joined on tenor saxophone for some songs, and Brian Thomas joined on trombone for others [2]\n- Reviewer says the performance reflects the very high level Soulive had reached by the end of 2012, with some classic old jams [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-12-30.akg483.flac16**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > R-44 > WAV (24/96k) [1]. Also: Taper credited as groundhog, with a 2012 shared recording numbered 273, using AKG 483 per filename [1]\n- **soulive2012-12-30.akg483.flac24**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > R-44 > WAV (24/96k) [2]. Also: This is a 24-bit transfer of the recording, not intended for burning to CD [2]",
